/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 99 0 R
/T (The United Nations Security Council \(UNSC\) is one of the six principal organs of the United Nations and bears the primary responsibility for maintaining international peace and security. Established in 1945 under the UN Charter, the Council consists of 15 members: five permanent members the United States, the United Kingdom, France, Russia, and China and ten non-permanent members elected by the UN General Assembly for two-year terms. The five permanent members possess veto power, enabling any one of them to block the adoption of substantive resolutions. The Security Council is empowered to investigate disputes, recommend peaceful means of settlement, authorize peacekeeping operations, impose sanctions, and, when necessary, authorize the use of force to address threats to international peace and security.)
/E (The United Nations Security Council \(UNSC\) is one of the six principal organs of the United Nations and bears the primary responsibility for maintaining international peace and security. Established in 1945 under the UN Charter, the Council consists of 15 members: five permanent members the United States, the United Kingdom, France, Russia, and China and ten non-permanent members elected by the UN General Assembly for two-year terms. The five permanent members possess veto power, enabling any one of them to block the adoption of substantive resolutions. The Security Council is empowered to investigate disputes, recommend peaceful means of settlement, authorize peacekeeping operations, impose sanctions, and, when necessary, authorize the use of force to address threats to international peace and security.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
282 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 99 0 R
/T (As the UN's principal decision-making body on matters of peace and security, the Security Council serves as a forum where member states negotiate responses to international crises. Its decisions, known as resolutions, are legally binding on all UN Member States under the UN Charter. The Council meets throughout the year to address emerging conflicts, humanitarian crises, terrorism, and other threats to global stability. While the Security Council has played a central role in conflict resolution and peacekeeping for decades, it also faces criticism regarding the use of the veto, unequal representation, and its ability to respond effectively to rapidly evolving geopolitical challenges. Nevertheless, it remains the most influential international body for promoting collective security and international cooperation.)
/E (As the UN's principal decision-making body on matters of peace and security, the Security Council serves as a forum where member states negotiate responses to international crises. Its decisions, known as resolutions, are legally binding on all UN Member States under the UN Charter. The Council meets throughout the year to address emerging conflicts, humanitarian crises, terrorism, and other threats to global stability. While the Security Council has played a central role in conflict resolution and peacekeeping for decades, it also faces criticism regarding the use of the veto, unequal representation, and its ability to respond effectively to rapidly evolving geopolitical challenges. Nevertheless, it remains the most influential international body for promoting collective security and international cooperation.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
