/T (The establishment of Israel in 1948 and the first Arab-Israeli War marked a major turning point in regional history. The conflict resulted in significant displacement and created lasting political disagreements that continue to influence relations between Israel, Palestine, and neighbouring states. Subsequent conflicts, including the Six-Day War in 1967 and the Yom Kippur War in 1973, further intensified regional tensions and shaped modern security concerns.)
/E (The establishment of Israel in 1948 and the first Arab-Israeli War marked a major turning point in regional history. The conflict resulted in significant displacement and created lasting political disagreements that continue to influence relations between Israel, Palestine, and neighbouring states. Subsequent conflicts, including the Six-Day War in 1967 and the Yom Kippur War in 1973, further intensified regional tensions and shaped modern security concerns.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
