/P 101 0 R
/T (During the Cold War, the Middle East became an area of competition between global powers. The United States and the Soviet Union supported different governments and political movements, increasing the international dimension of regional conflicts. Rivalries between major powers often influenced local disputes, making peaceful resolution more difficult.)
/E (During the Cold War, the Middle East became an area of competition between global powers. The United States and the Soviet Union supported different governments and political movements, increasing the international dimension of regional conflicts. Rivalries between major powers often influenced local disputes, making peaceful resolution more difficult.)
/Pg 16 0 R
