/P 101 0 R
/T (Following the end of the Cold War, the region experienced further instability. Events such as the Gulf War, the 2003 invasion of Iraq, the rise of extremist organizations such as ISIS, and the Arab Spring uprisings contributed to political uncertainty and weakened state institutions in several countries. These developments created conditions where armed groups gained influence and conflicts became increasingly difficult to contain.)
/E (Following the end of the Cold War, the region experienced further instability. Events such as the Gulf War, the 2003 invasion of Iraq, the rise of extremist organizations such as ISIS, and the Arab Spring uprisings contributed to political uncertainty and weakened state institutions in several countries. These developments created conditions where armed groups gained influence and conflicts became increasingly difficult to contain.)
