/E (In recent years, security challenges in the Middle East have become more interconnected. Rivalries involving Iran, Israel, Saudi Arabia, and various armed groups have contributed to instability in areas including Gaza, Lebanon, Syria, Iraq, and Yemen. The increasing use of drones, missile systems, and cyber capabilities has also changed the nature of modern conflict, allowing tensions to spread beyond traditional battlefields.)
