/P 106 0 R
/E (In 2019, widespread protests led to the removal of President Omar al-Bashir, who had ruled Sudan for nearly three decades. A transitional government involving civilian and military representatives was established with the goal of guiding the country toward democratic elections. However, disagreements between political and military leaders weakened the transition process.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
