/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 107 0 R
/T (As of 2026, Sudan remains affected by a devastating conflict between the Sudanese Armed Forces \(SAF\) and the Rapid Support Forces \(RSF\). The fighting, which began in April 2023, has resulted in widespread insecurity, a collapse of essential services, and one of the largest humanitarian emergencies in the world.)
/E (As of 2026, Sudan remains affected by a devastating conflict between the Sudanese Armed Forces \(SAF\) and the Rapid Support Forces \(RSF\). The fighting, which began in April 2023, has resulted in widespread insecurity, a collapse of essential services, and one of the largest humanitarian emergencies in the world.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
419 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (Millions of civilians have been forced to leave their homes due to ongoing violence, with many seeking safety in neighbouring countries such as Chad, Egypt, South Sudan, Ethiopia, and the Central African Republic. The scale of displacement has placed significant pressure on both humanitarian organizations and host communities, many of which are already facing economic and security challenges.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
420 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (Food insecurity has become one of the most urgent concerns in Sudan. Conflict has disrupted agricultural production, damaged markets, and restricted humanitarian access in many areas. Several regions have faced extreme levels of hunger due to continued fighting and difficulties delivering aid. The situation has been further worsened by economic instability and shortages of essential resources.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
421 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 107 0 R
/T <>
/E <>
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
422 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 107 0 R
/T (Serious concerns have also been raised regarding violations of international humanitarian law. Reports of attacks against civilians, conflict-related sexual violence, forced displacement, and destruction of civilian infrastructure have highlighted the urgent need for stronger protection measures and accountability mechanisms.)
/E (Serious concerns have also been raised regarding violations of international humanitarian law. Reports of attacks against civilians, conflict-related sexual violence, forced displacement, and destruction of civilian infrastructure have highlighted the urgent need for stronger protection measures and accountability mechanisms.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
423 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 107 0 R
/T (The conflict has divided control of Sudan between competing armed actors, with the SAF and RSF maintaining influence over different regions of the country. This fragmentation has made humanitarian operations increasingly difficult and has complicated international efforts to negotiate a lasting ceasefire.)
/E (The conflict has divided control of Sudan between competing armed actors, with the SAF and RSF maintaining influence over different regions of the country. This fragmentation has made humanitarian operations increasingly difficult and has complicated international efforts to negotiate a lasting ceasefire.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
