/E (The Sudan crisis has consequences beyond its borders. The movement of refugees, the spread of weapons, and political tensions in neighbouring countries have increased concerns about regional instability.Delegates should examine ways to support neighbouring states, strengthen border security cooperation, and prevent the conflict from contributing to wider insecurity in the Horn of Africa and Sahel regions.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
436 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 108 0 R
/E (Several international and regional actors, including the United Nations, African Union, and Intergovernmental Authority on Development \(IGAD\), have attempted to support negotiations between the SAF and RSF.However, achieving a lasting ceasefire remains difficult due to disagreements between the parties and continued military operations. Delegates should explore how mediation efforts can be strengthened and how ceasefire agreements can be monitored effectively.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
