/Title (The United Nations Security Council \(UNSC\) is one of the six principal organs of the United Nations and bears the primary responsibility for maintaining international peace and security. Established in 1945 under the UN Charter, the Council consists of 15 members: five permanent members the United States, the United Kingdom, France, Russia, and China and ten non-permanent members elected by the UN General Assembly for two-year terms. The five permanent members possess veto power, enabling any one of them to block the adoption of substantive resolutions. The Security Council is empowered to investigate disputes, recommend peaceful means of settlement, authorize peacekeeping operations, impose sanctions, and, when necessary, authorize the use of force to address threats to international peace and security.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1321 0 R
/Next 1386 0 R
>>
endobj
