/Title (As the UN's principal decision-making body on matters of peace and security, the Security Council serves as a forum where member states negotiate responses to international crises. Its decisions, known as resolutions, are legally binding on all UN Member States under the UN Charter. The Council meets throughout the year to address emerging conflicts, humanitarian crises, terrorism, and other threats to global stability. While the Security Council has played a central role in conflict resolution and peacekeeping for decades, it also faces criticism regarding the use of the veto, unequal representation, and its ability to respond effectively to rapidly evolving geopolitical challenges. Nevertheless, it remains the most influential international body for promoting collective security and international cooperation.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1321 0 R
/Prev 1372 0 R
/Next 1397 0 R
>>
endobj
1387 0 obj
